Content shell: tell sites what Chromium of this version tells them.

The shell's user agent was "Chrome/999.0.0.0" and its client hints the
brand "content_shell" 999 on platform "Unknown": a browser that does not
exist, named after a test tool. Sites take it for a bot or an unknown
browser (bot checks run harder, scripts take fallback paths). zebkit's
views are the shell's, so its user agent and client hints are now
Chromium's own, from embedder_support: the real version, the brands with
GREASE, the platform. --user-agent still overrides the string.

